  "worked_solution": "First, recall that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}f(s) & =\u27e8{lim}_{s\\to 0}{e}^{s},\\,{lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{{s}^{2}-2}{s+6},\\,{lim}_{s\\to 0}{4}^{s}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one-by-one.\n\n- For the first component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}{e}^{s} & ={e}^{0}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{{s}^{2}-2}{s+6} & =\\frac{{0}^{2}-2}{0+6} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}{4}^{s} & ={4}^{0}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{s\\to 0}f(s)=\u27e81,\\,-\\frac{1}{3},\\,1\u27e9.$\n\nFinally, the limit of $\u2016f(s)\u2016$ as $s$ approaches $0$ is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}\u2016f(s)\u2016 & =\u2016{lim}_{s\\to 0}f(s)\u2016 \\\\  & =\u2016\u27e81,\\,-\\frac{1}{3},\\,1\u27e9\u2016 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{9}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{19}{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
